      "concern": "The Statement, lines 34–35, says only that 'each' worker gradient averages b independent uniform component gradients. It does not explicitly require independence across workers or independence of current draws from the earlier history. The proof's Given instead asserts 'mutually independent uniform indices in the Statement', and Step 1.1 uses independence of every distinct draw. Without the cross-worker requirement the stated 1/K reduction is false: take n=K=2, b=1, scalar f₁(x)=x and f₂(x)=−x, both worker points fixed at zero, σ²=1, and use the same fresh uniform component index for both workers. Every worker batch satisfies the written sampling condition, but E|g_t−ḡ_t|²=1>1/2. The mutually independent sampling in alg-local-sgd and in thm-local-sgd-convex-round-complexity supports the intended result; the standalone lemma's Statement needs that scope made explicit.",
